<code>assert !Objects.isNull(coll) => this.size() == coll.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i &amp;&amp; i < coll.size(); this.get(i).equals(coll.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the input collection `coll` is not null, the constructed `TreeList` has the same size as the collection and that each element in the `TreeList` matches the corresponding element in the collection.
--------------------
<code>assert CollectionUtils.isEqualCollection(this, coll);</code>

However, since we need to use only publicly accessible observer methods and avoid direct calls to methods like `CollectionUtils.isEqualCollection`, we can use the `size` and `contains` methods to construct the assertion:

<code>assert coll != null && this.size() == coll.size() && \forall Object o; coll.contains(o); this.contains(o);</code>

This ensures that the constructed `TreeList` has the same elements and size as the input collection `coll`.
